<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Shinji</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Shinji is a brackish lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimane-prefecture">Shimane Prefecture</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and one of the largest lakes in the country. Linked to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a> through Lake Nakaumi, it lies beside the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matsue">Matsue</a>, whose castle was built near its shore in the early seventeenth century. It is known for its sunsets and its shijimi clams.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-shinji.jpg" alt="Lake Shinji" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 江戸村のとくぞう · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matsue_Castle-4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
